<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles III of Navarre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1361">1361</a>–1425</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Charles III the Noble</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles III the Noble was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> from 1387, of the French house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evreux">Évreux</a>. Unlike his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-navarre">Charles the Bad</a>, he kept peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, exchanging his Norman claims for the duchy of Nemours. He reorganised the kingdom's administration, united the boroughs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a> in 1423, and built the palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olite">Olite</a> and the cathedral cloister of Pamplona.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-navarre.jpg" alt="Charles III of Navarre" width="320" height="508" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karel3_Evreux_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Charles III the Noble</b> (1387–1425) built the palace of Olite and in 1423 united the three rival boroughs of Pamplona by the Privilege of the Union.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-navarre">Kingdom of Navarre · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1404 his son <b>Charles III of Navarre</b> exchanged Évreux with Charles VI for the duchy of Nemours, and it returned to the Kingdom of France.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-evreux">County of Évreux</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olite">Olite/Erriberri</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=47.22,-1.55&amp;year=1402" aria-label="Nantes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4514 507 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Charles III of Navarre"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4964 777h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4964 777h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=47.22,-1.55&amp;year=1402">What was here in 1402? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
